==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)pend-}}
From stem of {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|expenditus}}, irregular perfect passive participle of {{m|la|expendo||I weigh, I pay out}}, {{suffix|en||ure|gloss2=process or result}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ɛkˈspɛndɪt͡ʃɚ/|/ɪkˈspɛndɪt͡ʃɚ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɛkˈspɛndɪt͡ʃə/|/ɪkˈspɛndɪt͡ʃə/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-expenditure.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyph|en|ex|pen|di|ture}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} Act of [[expend]]ing or [[pay]]ing out.
# {{lb|en|uncountable|countable}} The [[amount]] [[expend]]ed; [[expense]]; outlay.
#: ''The '''expenditure''' of time, money, and political capital on this project has been excessive.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|act of expending}}
* {{sense|amount expended}} {{l|en|disbursement}}, {{l|en|expense}}, {{l|en|payment}}, {{l|en|cost}}, {{l|en|charge}}, {{l|en|outlay}}

